Timeout! Something is hanging. Probably an infinite loop in my chunk-boundary keep loop, or in the reading loop. Let me think.

`br.Read(buf)` — buf starts as nil; bufio.Reader.Read: if the internal buffer is empty, fill it from r; then copy. If the underlying reader always returns (n>0, nil) with a fixed ch... no, EOF will come eventually.

Hmm, the infinite loop might be in the trailing-keep loop. Let me examine:

```go
for off := 0; off < 3 && off < len(buf); off++ {
	c := buf[len(buf)-1-off]
	...
	if len(buf)-(len(buf)-1-off) < need {
		keep := len(buf) - 1 - off
		buf = append([]byte{}, buf[keep:]...)
		break
	}
	break
